Subject: [PATCH] provider: bound rollback after child callback insertion failure

If all provider creation callbacks succeed but pushing the child callback
registration fails, i equals the provider count. Starting rollback there
passes a NULL provider to remove_cb, which can dereference it when obtaining
its name. Start at the last visited provider instead. Keep including the
current provider when its creation callback fails partway through the loop.
An empty provider list must not invoke a removal callback.

--- a/crypto/provider_core.c
+++ b/crypto/provider_core.c
@@ -2186,6 +2186,8 @@ static int ossl_provider_register_child_cb(const OSSL_CORE_HANDLE *handle,
     }
     if (i != max || ret <= 0) {
         /* Failed during creation. Remove everything we just added */
+        if (i == max)
+            --i;
         for (; i >= 0; i--) {
             prov = sk_OSSL_PROVIDER_value(store->providers, i);
             remove_cb((OSSL_CORE_HANDLE *)prov, cbdata);
